{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"4a6b7eec3cd0ff92784240b1e7c3ab99f5d2374d58566b3ef444dbb30a70b8ff","packTokens":3728,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"platform","tokens":215,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":627,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":1253,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":1528,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"PLATFORM. This product is designed and built as a web app, and nothing else. Where the requirements ask for a mobile app, a phone app, an iOS or Android app, treat them as the same features in one responsive web app that works well on a phone's browser: never stop, park, ask or leave a requirement out because it names a mobile app, and never plan a native app, an app store step or a phone-only frame. Every page is responsive: it is laid out for a phone, a tablet and a desktop width, with touch-sized controls on the narrow one. What only a native app can do (push notifications, background location, a home-screen icon) is given its closest web form (an in-app notice or email, the browser's location prompt, an installable web app) and said so.\n\nMap each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Replace the current manual processes with a single platform covering stock, orders, deliveries, live temperature monitoring, quality decisions and recalls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-2\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a responsive web portal for warehouse staff, dispatchers, quality staff, administrators and auditors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a customer portal for hospitals, pharmacies and clinics.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"Provide a driver experience that keeps working without a connection.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"Receive temperature readings from data loggers and cold-room sensors.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-6\",\n  \"text\": \"Keep a centralized shared record of stock, orders and temperature history.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-7\",\n  \"text\": \"Support secure sign-in, role and warehouse access controls, customer-organization isolation, and read-only auditor access.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-8\",\n  \"text\": \"Define versioned product temperature profiles and stability budgets.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-9\",\n  \"text\": \"Receive stock by lot, track inbound logger readings, quarantine stock, and release it through quality review.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-10\",\n  \"text\": \"Let customer users place, view, change and cancel orders under the specified delivery and order rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-11\",\n  \"text\": \"Allocate released stock to orders by earliest expiry while respecting shelf-life, availability and order-completion rules.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-12\",\n  \"text\": \"Pack stock into qualified shipper boxes and plan routes with drivers and vehicles.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-13\",\n  \"text\": \"Store and process delayed, duplicated and out-of-order temperature readings reliably.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-14\",\n  \"text\": \"Detect excursions, charge stability budgets, place affected stock on hold, and alert relevant users.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-15\",\n  \"text\": \"Enable drivers to load, drive and record delivery handovers using their phone, including offline use.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-16\",\n  \"text\": \"Support the portals in English and Arabic, with Arabic displayed right to left.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-17\",\n  \"text\": \"Track recalled lots, block remaining stock and account for customer responses.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"What must the full two-person quality decision for stock exposed to a not-permitted temperature range require?\",\n  \"answer\": \"A Quality Officer proposes the disposition and a different Quality Manager approves it; neither person can perform both steps.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"When an excursion opens, how quickly must affected stock be placed On Hold relative to the alert deadline?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Place it On Hold as soon as the excursion is detected; the two-minute deadline applies to alerts.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"What customer evidence must the driver record for a delivery handover?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Record the recipient's name and an explicit electronic acknowledgment of receipt; a drawn signature is not required.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen to quantities that are not handed over because a delivery is refused or only partly completed?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Keep undelivered quantities outstanding; record the reason and return them to available stock only after warehouse receipt and any required quality checks.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"What constitutes a handling unit for tracking stability budgets when a received quantity is split, moved, or packed into different boxes?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Track quantities as handling units and split the record whenever portions acquire different temperature histories.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-6\",\n  \"question\": \"Who may maintain a customer organisation's saved delivery addresses and minimum remaining shelf-life requirement?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Customer Administrators maintain their organisation's addresses; System Administrators set its minimum shelf life.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-7\",\n  \"question\": \"How should the stock quantity breakdown reconcile with quantity on hand, given that stock can also be On Hold, Rejected, Recalled or Expired?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Treat on-hand as the total and show a mutually exclusive breakdown that includes available, allocated, quarantined and the other stock statuses.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-8\",\n  \"question\": \"When a product profile changes with an effective date, how should the new profile affect stock already received and its temperature-budget history?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Apply the new version to stock still held from its effective date onward and recalculate affected budgets and decisions from that date.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"answer\": \"Yes: \\\"The system shall be sized for 5,000 devices reporting at once.\\\"\",\n  \"by\": \"factory\",\n  \"id\": \"Q-13\",\n  \"question\": \"Does the request ask for this: Support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox, and support the stated first-year user and record volume and simultaneous device volume.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-9\",\n  \"question\": \"The 28 requirements are estimated at about four runs of work. How would you like the scope handled?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Split the full scope across about four runs; keep all requirements.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-10\",\n  \"question\": \"What should happen to unsynchronized driver actions when a driver signs out or the API reports the account disabled, especially if another user later signs in on the same browser?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Retain unsynchronized actions in a queue tied to the originating driver; sync only after that same driver signs in again, and erase or reject the queue if access is refused or the account is disabled.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-11\",\n  \"question\": \"When a temperature-history gap affects stock, should the stock be automatically placed On Hold while the gap is unresolved, or should the gap be flagged for review without automatically changing stock status?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Flag the gap for review and show the API-returned stock status; do not automatically place the stock On Hold.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-12\",\n  \"question\": \"May a temperature-profile version have an effective date in the past, and if so, how should recalculated results affect stock that was already released or had a quality decision?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Require effective dates to be today or later; do not recalculate earlier decisions.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Build the Meridian responsive web app with role-oriented portal pages for stock, orders, deliveries, temperature monitoring, quality decisions, and recalls, responsive across phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Provide staff sign-in through Meridian Microsoft accounts and customer sign-in by email, password, and one-time code, plus email password-reset links; do not offer customer social sign-in or single sign-on.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Show users only role-, warehouse-, and organisation-authorized records and actions, make Auditor views read-only, and clear protected data when access is refused.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Provide Customer Administrators with organisation-scoped controls to invite and remove users and maintain saved delivery addresses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Provide System Administrators with product search, viewing, deactivation, maintenance, and versioned temperature-profile management, including validated tiers, reason, effective date, and read-only earlier versions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Display effective profile changes and API-returned recalculated budgets, decisions, and affected stock, order, box, and route statuses while leaving earlier quality decisions unchanged.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Provide receipt capture for product, lot, expiry, quantity, supplier, and storage location; support inbound logger files and separate image or PDF evidence; and show returned quarantine, temperature, and budget information before release.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Provide quality staff with receipt and excursion review, release and disposition controls, and separate proposal and approval steps for not-permitted-range dispositions.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Show on-hand stock quantities by mutually exclusive status with returned warehouse, lot, product, receipt, and location details, and show separate handling units when their temperature histories differ.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Provide stock-movement forms and show returned source and destination locations, quantity, actor, and time.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Let System Administrators set an organisation's minimum remaining shelf-life requirement and show it read-only to customer users and Dispatchers.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Let customers create orders with product lines, pack quantities, saved addresses, eligible delivery dates, and a partial-or-complete delivery preference; show order summaries, statuses, allocations, and outstanding quantities.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"Provide customer order changes and cancellations only before Packed, dispatcher cancellations when available, retry-safe order submission, dispatcher lot overrides with required reasons, and returned allocation and stock-status outcomes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Let Warehouse Operators pack stock into shipper boxes with a box type, one logger per box, delivery stop, products, lots, and quantities; show returned compatibility and sealing details.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"Let Dispatchers create and view routes with a date, vehicle, driver, ordered stops, and planned arrival times, and show returned confirmation errors, safety margins, route changes, and driver notifications.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Show box, cold-room, and lot temperature histories in chart and table views, including returned readings, applicable bands, excursions, gaps, flags, and silence status.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Show returned excursions, handling-unit budget use and remaining allowances, alerts, hold and decision statuses, and unresolved temperature-history gaps without inferring a hold or estimated temperature tier or charge.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Show returned quality-review cases for corrected temperature history affecting stock already delivered.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Provide an installable responsive driver experience that caches the current workday's assigned route, queues supported offline actions for synchronization by the originating driver, clears protected cached data when required, and shows stale-route and queued-action outcomes.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"Provide delivery handover capture for recipient name, explicit electronic acknowledgment, handed-over quantities, and refusal or partial-delivery reasons, and show outstanding quantities and returned delivery and quality statuses.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Let Quality Managers start, view, manage, and close recalls, and let customers reconcile quantities and stated dispositions for affected deliveries without requiring supporting-document uploads.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Provide filtered operational lists and CSV export, and show returned creator and last-changer identities and timestamps as read-only metadata.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Provide English and Arabic portal content, rendering Arabic right to left and English left to right.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Ensure pages reflow across phone, tablet, and desktop browser widths, with touch-sized controls on narrow layouts, conform to WCAG 2.1 Level AA for main staff, customer, and driver flows, support the latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari, and Firefox, and support the stated first-year user and record volume and simultaneous device volume.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}